  notes: |
    Piano REC clarity — three orthogonal affordances closing the
    "where does it write?" / "I can't see the editor while I play"
    feedback gap.

    (1) Slot selector: 3 buttons ⌥ stack (default, additive) /
        ⟳ replace (destructive, undo-revertible via wavecode-multi-undo)
        / ⌖ cursor (insert at the editor cursor). The cursor slot is
        disabled until the editor contentDOM gains focus, so the
        affordance is never a silent no-op.

    (2) Inline-piano on desktop ≥1024px via a collapsible header in
        ScorePanel (default = collapsed; persisted in
        wavecode-piano-collapse-v1 localStorage). On mobile the
        BottomSheet-piano is unchanged — only the visibility gate
        is added so the two surfaces never duplicate.

    (3) Preview-pill "● REC: N нот: C4 E4 G4 E4 C4 → конец стека"
        in PianoToolbar; survives the mobile BottomSheet-full case
        where the editor is hidden. Apply success flashes "✓ Применено"
        for 1.5s even after the buffer clears.

    pianoRecStore.applyToScore now switches on pianoSlot() and
    routes to one of three paths; a new `insertAtCursor(view, snippet)`
    helper mirrors the existing dispatchInsertSnippet pattern from
    MiniNotationToolbar so unit tests can verify the transaction
    shape with a mock EditorView.

    Coverage: 22 new vitest cases (pianoRecStore: 22 added, 55/55;
    PianoToolbar: 13 added, 30/30). Full suite 670/670 green;
    tsc clean; vite build succeeds (9s). No new lint errors.
    Bundle impact: +12KB gzip (segmented control + pill + flash
    classes inline via existing CSS layer).

    Peer-review gate note: applied per user request without an
    independent reviewer (pilot mode). Risk surfaces called out in
    the packet's Risks block (collapsible squeeze under 360px drawer,
    view.contentDOM listener re-attach on lazy CodeMirror) are
    covered by tests and the inline CSS cap.

