  notes: |
    Polish pass — closes two outstanding items from the packet's
    "Что осталось вне scope" block.

    (a) **Flash-decoration hook**. CodeMirror-side highlight on the
        inserted lines after a successful apply, driven by a new
        `flashDecorations` StateField in pianoRecStore
        (`setFlashDecorations` / `clearFlashDecorations` StateEffects
        + `buildFlashRange` pure line-resolution helper + `flashRange`
        side-effect). Registered in `CodeMirrorEditorImpl` extensions
        alongside `miniNotationHighlight` + `runtimeMiniHighlight`.
        All three applyToScore branches flash:
          - replace-score → entire new doc
          - at-cursor     → inserted line range
          - append-stack  → entire new doc (post-dispatch)
        Capped at 10 lines per range via `FLASH_LINE_CAP` so a
        100-line recording doesn't paint 100 simultaneous decorations.

    (b) **TabBar Piano desktop-hidden**. `.wc-tab[aria-label='Piano']`
        has `display: none` in a `@media (min-width: 1024px)` block —
        on desktop the tab was a dead no-op (BottomSheet-piano is
        gated to mobile in the same packet). Mobile keeps the tab
        because that's where BottomSheet-piano lives.

    New coverage: 4 new vitest cases (buildFlashRange pure-builder
    + StateEffect exports). 1 new e2e spec (`piano-rec-slot.spec.ts`,
    6 cases): append-stack, replace-score + undo, at-cursor + focus,
    preview-pill state, desktop inline toggle, mobile BottomSheet.
    Full suite 694/694 green; tsc clean; vite build 10.2s.

    Layout follow-up (not in this polish): user feedback indicates
    the broader TabBar affordance — "sheets should push the editor
    rather than cover it" — needs a separate packet. Tracked under
    the proposed `wavecode-sheets-aside-editor` direction.